The '''Mission Saint Augustine of Xaraba''' ({{langx|an|Misión Sant Agustín de Xaraba}}) is a historic [[W:Basilicas in the Catholic Church|Catholic basilica]] complex in [[Sant Agustín]], [[Xaraba]], [[Bayara]]. It is dedicated to [[W:Augustine of Hippo|Augustine of Hippo]], the historic [[W:Patron saint|patron]] of Bayara. Operated by the [[Archdiocese of Sant Agustín]], the complex was founded in the 17th century by [[United Kingdoms of Volisania|Volisanian]] Catholic missionaries. The mission contains two historic buildings:

* The Mission adobe chapel, constructed in 1638. It is the oldest structure in Sant Agustín.
* The Basílica de San Agustín de Xaraba, constructed in 1868 and designated a [[W:Minor basilica|minor basilica]] by Pope Pius XII in 1952.

